# Line-ending normalisation for a corpus whose whole purpose is to be copied into other
# repositories (#109). 534 Markdown files and 12 shell scripts travel into repositories on other
# platforms; without this, a contributor on Windows produces a diff that touches every line of a
# file, and the link, frontmatter and mutation checks then read content their editor rewrote.
#
# Normalise everything textual in the repository, and store LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts must be LF wherever they land: a CRLF shebang line makes the interpreter unfindable.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf diff=python

# Markdown carries 34 lines that end in two deliberate spaces (a hard line break). They are
# content, not whitespace noise — see .editorconfig, which tells editors not to strip them.
*.md    text

# Binaries an adopting repository brings with it. This corpus ships none today; the marks exist
# because this file is copied into repositories that do, and a mangled PNG is silent damage.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
